<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.BootstrapModel
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:relation="org.blockml.bml.relation"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <idea>README.bml, Bootstrap role, references with ReadFirst, and interpretation context.</idea>

  <documentation>
    Self-hosting bootstrap: the compiler loads framework BML from @blockml/core (and domain
    packages) before user content — TypeRegistry bootstrap, not special-cased type semantics
    in code.

    Bootstrap order (summary):
    1. Core branches — Block, ValueType, Language, Status, Relation, Constraint, Capability, Definition
    2. Concrete types — Integer, Decimal, languages, services, constraints, relations
    3. BlockLibrary — library descriptor base (bootstrap, _dependencies, _subLibraries, _schemas, _blocks)
    4. org.blockml.bml.Library — published catalog via _blocks; bootstrap → README
    5. Domain framework BML (e.g. com.machineblocks.bml.core.*)

    org.blockml.bml.core.Bootstrap is an abstract role marker — a library or process entry point.
    org.blockml.bml.README is the standard human/LLM subtype. Library.bml declares the entry via
    the bootstrap aggregation (typically &lt;blockml:README /&gt;). Other Bootstrap subtypes may
    follow for agents, CI pipelines, or TypeRegistry loaders.

    Curated reading order lives in &lt;references&gt; on the concrete Bootstrap block — each entry
    uses relation=ReadFirst with a context note. Available tasks use relation=TaskIndex on the
    same references container. One mechanism for all cross-links; tooling filters by relation.
    No separate readFirst or tasks aggregation on Bootstrap.

    Task-oriented paths:
    • org.blockml.bml.core.TaskGuide — procedural org.blockml.bml.task.* blocks
    • relation=TaskStep — ordered steps inside a TaskGuide (document order)
    • relation=Prerequisite — before starting a task
    • org.blockml.bml.core.Diagnostic — org.blockml.bml.diagnostic.* validator codes
    • relation=Resolves — Diagnostic → TaskGuide fix procedure

    Interpretation context:
    • Framework BML defines what types ARE — TypeRegistry SSOT
    • Renderers interpret what types MEAN for their target — free manifestation
    • README references with ReadFirst establish shared vocabulary before diving into definitions
    • After the first ten ReadFirst documentation blocks, most of the core library can be derived
      directly from Block definitions themselves

    Each registered BlockDefinition from bootstrap is an immutable BomDocument parse result.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="16_framework_base_types.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
      Bootstrap Order — framework BML load sequence for TypeRegistry.
    </see>
    <see file="13_bml_to_bom_mapping.md" relation="AuthoringGuide">
